// The wall KITS, baked into assets/buildings/wall-kits.pak by tools/gc_artbake
// (`cargo run -p gc_artbake --release -- --config assets-src/buildings/wall-kits.ron --out assets/buildings/wall-kits.pak`).
// Separate pieces a seeded generator lays along each drawn, curved wall tile (docs/29 "Dynamic bridges in brief",
// curved walls; docs/26): names starting "Palisade Kit " (Ember) and "Bone Fence Kit " (Carrion Concord). They
// dress no building (the test `building_models_dress_buildings` allows both prefixes). Names fit the 24-byte field.
// Conventions, as for the bridge kit: every piece keeps its authored position (keep_origin); 1 tile = 1 unit;
// origin at z = 0 on the ground the game draws, the wall's centre line at x = 0; a run is exactly 1 tile long
// along the model's z (y -0.5 .. 0.5 in Blender, which the glTF turns into -z), so tiles meet end to end; posts
// stand on a tile joint (centred on the origin); one-sided pieces have their FRONT (outside) towards +x, the
// back (rails, walkway, braces, plainer face) towards -x; turn a piece half a turn about the vertical for the
// other side. Each atlas is its own set of five maps (the game shrinks every material to 512 px).
//   Ember Palisade (logs 1.40-1.56 tall, set 0.08 into the ground; front row x +0.075, back row x -0.075):
//     runs: "Palisade Kit Run A|B|C|D" (1 tile, differing log count, thickness, height, lean and tips),
//           "Palisade Kit Half Run" (0.5 tile along z, for a diagonal fill);
//     posts: "Palisade Kit Post" (1.6 tall, on a joint), "Palisade Kit End Post" (2.4 with pennon and banner,
//           stone block), "Palisade Kit Run Broken" (snapped, leaning, missing logs), "Palisade Kit Run Burnt"
//           (charred, with embers);
//     works: "Palisade Kit Walkway" (back side fighting step, deck top 0.82, x -0.66 .. -0.14),
//           "Palisade Kit Brace" (back buttress, x -0.95 .. -0.12, only 0.16 wide along z: one per tile or two),
//           overlays laid over a run: "Palisade Kit Footing" (stone footing, top 0.25, x +-0.34) and
//           "Palisade Kit Bands" (iron straps and spikes on the front, x 0.135 .. 0.27).
//   Concord Bone Fence (level 1 1.2 tall, thickness 0.3; level 2 "Ossuary Wall" 1.65, 0.6; level 3 2.1, 0.7;
//     the front +x carries bone ends, skulls and niches, the back is plainer):
//     "Bone Fence Kit Post|End|Run A|Run B|Run C|Broken" (level 1; End has a team banner),
//     "Bone Fence Kit L2 Post|End|Run A|Run B|Broken" (stacked bone bound in iron),
//     "Bone Fence Kit L3 Post|End|Run A|Run B|Broken" (lantern-lit niches; the post has a lantern on its front).
// Sources: the project's design/buildings/source/buildings/{ember,concord}/wall_kit/ (wall_kit.py, build_set.py,
// bake_kit.py, gen_ron.py).
